To Whom It May Concern,

Please consider this a formal notification that Kroger is deducting $4,200.00 from the next payment cycle against your March 2025 invoice batch.

Reason for deduction:
On orders PO-88421 and PO-88422, we received incorrect products on three SKUs (SKU-0043, SKU-0051, SKU-1181). The items received did not match the descriptions on the ASN and our stores have reported product that does not match the shelf specs.

Specific issues:
- SKU-0043: Received 12-pk bottles labeled as cans — wrong packaging format
- SKU-0051: Wrong flavor variant — received original, ordered zero sugar
- SKU-1181: Cases were 24-pk, we ordered 12-pk

The $4,200 deduction covers:
- Cost of return freight: $1,100
- Labor for re-sort and re-stock: $650
- Lost sales during the gap period (per our vendor agreement §7.4): $2,450

We require a formal response within 10 business days. We reserve the right to return all affected product for full credit if not resolved.

